From 5476f7113d0e906733e12b561a7972128773ee95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The people of the maps beside the player's on the wider field
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The DS makes a map's people (map objects: NPCs, berry trees, signs) as
the player walks into its map header and drops those of the map left,
all out of its screen; on the 3DS's wider field they popped in and out.
The people of the maps beside the player's are now there ahead
(MAP_OBJ_STATUS_PORT_NEIGHBOUR): FieldMap_PortNeighbours brings those in
reach from their map's events (MapHeaderData_PortObjectEvents), one a
frame, while there's room for their pictures (MapObjectGfx_PortHasRoom)
and for the game's own, and drops those out of reach. At the zone change
the map left's in reach stay beside (sub_0206184C), and the new map's
are taken as the game's own (MapObjectMan_AddMapObjectFromHeader). They
walk and are in the way, but can't be talked to, don't see the player,
aren't found by a script's local ID and aren't saved: as on the DS, where
they weren't there yet. Only while the field is wider than the DS's,
outside the Distortion World and the gyms' dynamic maps.
